Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Suppressing Uncoupled Singlets (Isolated Spins & Solvent)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e0f338e4-fa04-bf42-9807-be518c0ee6c7"],

Cell["\<\
Another major benefit of DQF-COSY is suppression of uncoupled spins (such as \
residual solvent signals or methyl singlets). An isolated spin-1/2 cannot \
support two-spin double-quantum coherence (|p| = 2 requires at least two \
coupled spins!), so it is completely eliminated by the double-quantum filter.

To demonstrate this, we add a third uncoupled spin-1/2 at +30 Hz to our AX \
pair and compare COSY-90 against both ideal CoherenceOrderFiltration DQF-COSY \
and 4-step PhaseCycle DQF-COSY.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b6457c9-ef54-e14c-bc76-13f0ec7c8e27"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SetSpinSystem", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"H3", "=", 
   RowBox[{"2.", "*", "Pi", "*", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "120."}], "*", 
       RowBox[{"opI", "[", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "\"\<z\>\""}], "]"}]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"180.", "*", 
