Cell["\<\
Notice how the 32 Hz Lorentzian broadening (exceeding J = 24 Hz) both \
broadens the multiplet lobes and suppresses the overall peak amplitude by \
destructive cancellation between opposite-sign components, whereas \
{\"SineBell\", Pi/4} retains sharp resolution and suppresses t1/t2 truncation \
wiggles.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f106c8a-5da9-c54b-bc05-7ad849620cc4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8. Summary: COSY-90 vs. DQF-COSY", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"23bd8f95-2e43-fd4d-8d85-53b22a6e122a"],

Cell["\<\
When designing a 2D homonuclear correlation simulation in SpinDynamica:
  1. Use CoherenceOrderFiltration[{-2, 2}] inside Mixing for exact, fast \
Hilbert-space double-quantum filtering, or use PhaseCycle when modeling real \
spectrometer phase tables.
  2. For 90_x - t1 - 90_x - DQF - 90_x with QuadratureMethod -> \"States\" \
(or \"StatesTPPI\" / \"EchoAntiEcho\"), apply PhaseCorrection -> {Pi/2, Pi/2} \
so both diagonal and cross peaks appear in pure anti-phase absorption in \"RR\
\".
  3. Keep total line broadening small compared to the active coupling J to \
avoid anti-phase self-cancellation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a3c37224-0bdb-7e4d-b0fc-8fa10179f7ba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"Feature\"\>", "\<\"COSY-90 (2 Pulses)\"\>", "\<\"DQF-COSY (3 Pulses \
+ p = +/-2 Filter)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Pulse sequence\"\>", "\<\"90_x - t1 - 90_x - t2\"\>", "\<\"90_x - \
t1 - 90_x - [DQF] - 90_x - t2\"\>"},
    {"\<\"SpinDynamica Mixing\"\>", "\<\"Mixing -> Pulse[{Pi/2, \\\"x\\\"}]\"\
\>", "\<\"Mixing -> {Pulse[{Pi/2, \\\"x\\\"}], CoherenceOrderFiltration[{-2, \
2}], Pulse[{Pi/2, \\\"x\\\"}]}\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Experimental cycle\"\>", "\<\"None needed for basic 2-pulse \
coherence\"\>", "\<\"4-step PhaseCycle on read pulse (or prep + 2nd \
pulse)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"States PhaseCorrection\"\>", "\<\"{0, 0} (cross peaks) or {Pi/2, \
Pi/2} (diagonal)\"\>", "\<\"{Pi/2, Pi/2} (all peaks simultaneously)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Diagonal lineshape\"\>", "\<\"In-phase (dispersive tails when cross \
peaks are absorptive)\"\>", "\<\"Pure anti-phase absorption (no dispersive \
wings)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Cross-peak lineshape\"\>", "\<\"Pure anti-phase absorption\"\>", \
"\<\"Pure anti-phase absorption (active: anti-phase; passive: \
in-phase)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Uncoupled singlets\"\>", "\<\"Strong dispersive diagonal peak\"\>", \
"\<\"Suppressed completely (cannot form p = +/-2)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Sensitivity & linewidth\"\>", "\<\"Full 2-pulse intensity\"\>", "\<\
\"50% theoretical amplitude; vanishes if linewidth >> J\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       GrayLevel[0.85], {
        GrayLevel[1], 
        RGBColor[0.97, 0.98, 1.]}}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"9c7989c4-d71b-0e47-bd49-ebdffff81dc4"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
